1. [THEOREM] Real Power Integral Formula: $\int_a^b x^r \, dx = \frac{b^{r+1} - a^{r+1}}{r+1}$ for $r > -1$ or $r \neq -1$ and $0 \notin [a,b]$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals
Name: integral_rpow
Description: For any real number $r$ such that either $r > -1$ or ($r \neq -1$ and $0 \notin [a, b]$), the integral of $x^r$ from $a$ to $b$ is given by:
\[
\int_a^b x^r \, dx = \frac{b^{r+1} - a^{r+1}}{r+1}.
\]
Signature:  {r : ℝ} (h : -1 < r ∨ r ≠ -1 ∧ (0 : ℝ) ∉ [[a, b]]) : ∫ x in a..b, x ^ r = (b ^ (r + 1) - a ^ (r + 1)) / (r + 1)

2. [THEOREM] Interval integrability of $x^r$ for $r > -1$ with Lebesgue measure
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals
Name: intervalIntegral.intervalIntegrable_rpow'
Description: For any real number $r > -1$, the function $x \mapsto x^r$ is interval integrable on any interval $[a, b]$ with respect to the Lebesgue measure.
Signature:  {r : ℝ} (h : -1 < r) : IntervalIntegrable (fun x => x ^ r) volume a b

3. [THEOREM] Square Root as Power: $\sqrt{x} = x^{1/2}$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real
Name: Real.sqrt_eq_rpow
Description: For any real number $x$, the square root of $x$ is equal to $x$ raised to the power of $1/2$, i.e., $\sqrt{x} = x^{1/2}$.
Signature:  (x : ℝ) : √x = x ^ (1 / (2 : ℝ))
