Module: Mathlib.Order.ConditionallyCompleteLattice.Finset
Name: Finset.sup_univ_eq_ciSup
Description: For a finite type $\iota$ and a function $f \colon \iota \to \alpha$ where $\alpha$ is a conditionally complete lattice, the supremum of $f$ over the universal finset (containing all elements of $\iota$) is equal to the indexed supremum of $f$ over $\iota$, i.e., 
\[ \sup_{i \in \text{univ}} f(i) = \bigsqcup_{i \in \iota} f(i). \]
