2. [DEFINITION] Locally finite order from finite closed intervals
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Defs
Name: LocallyFiniteOrder.ofFiniteIcc
Description: Given a preorder $(α, \leq)$ where all closed intervals $[a,b] = \{x \in α \mid a \leq x \leq b\}$ are finite for any $a, b \in α$, this constructs a locally finite order structure on $α$. The construction is noncomputable and uses the axiom of choice to convert the finite sets into finsets.
Signature:  (h : ∀ a b : α, (Set.Icc a b).Finite) : LocallyFiniteOrder α

