7. [INSTANCE] Locally Finite Order with Top from Locally Finite Order
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Defs
Name: LocallyFiniteOrder.toLocallyFiniteOrderTop
Description: Every locally finite order with a top element is also a locally finite order where all intervals bounded below are finite. Specifically, for any preorder $\alpha$ that is locally finite and has a top element $\top$, the structure of `LocallyFiniteOrderTop` is automatically satisfied, meaning that for any $a \in \alpha$, the intervals $[a, \top]$ and $(a, \top]$ can be represented as finite sets.
Signature:  : LocallyFiniteOrderTop α

8. [THEOREM] Antitonicity of the "less than or equal to $x$" predicate
Module: Mathlib.Order.BoundedOrder.Monotone
Name: antitone_le
Description: For any element $x$ in a preorder $\alpha$, the function that checks whether an element is less than or equal to $x$ (i.e., $(\cdot \leq x)$) is antitone. That is, for any $a, b \in \alpha$, if $a \leq b$, then $(b \leq x) \to (a \leq x)$.
Signature:  {x : α} : Antitone (· ≤ x)
