1. [THEOREM] Integral of $x^{-1}$: $\int_{a}^{b} \frac{1}{x} \, dx = \log(b/a)$ for $0 \notin [a, b]$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals
Name: integral_inv
Description: For real numbers $a$ and $b$ such that $0$ is not in the closed interval between $a$ and $b$ (i.e., $0 \notin [a, b]$), the integral of $x^{-1}$ from $a$ to $b$ equals the natural logarithm of the ratio $b/a$, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} \frac{1}{x} \, dx = \log\left(\frac{b}{a}\right). \]
Signature:  (h : (0 : ℝ) ∉ [[a, b]]) : ∫ x in a..b, x⁻¹ = log (b / a)

2. [THEOREM] Integral of Antitone Function on Interval Bounded by Sum Over Integer Points
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons
Name: AntitoneOn.integral_le_sum_Ico
Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be an antitone (decreasing) function on the closed interval $[a, b]$, where $a \leq b$. Then the integral of $f$ over $[a, b]$ is bounded above by the sum of $f$ evaluated at the integer points in the half-open interval $[a, b)$, i.e.,
\[
\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, dx \leq \sum_{x \in [a, b) \cap \mathbb{Z}} f(x).
\]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : AntitoneOn f (Set.Icc a b)) : (∫ x in a..b, f x) ≤ ∑ x ∈ Finset.Ico a b, f x

