1. [THEOREM] Denominator Formula for Rational Numbers: $\text{den}(n/d) = |d|/\gcd(n,d)$ (with $1$ if $d=0$)
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Lemmas
Name: Rat.den_mk
Description: For any integers $n$ and $d$, the denominator of the rational number $n/d$ (in reduced form) is given by:
\[
\text{den}(n/d) = \begin{cases}
1 & \text{if } d = 0, \\
\frac{|d|}{\gcd(n,d)} & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\]
Signature:  (n d : ℤ) : (n /. d).den = if d = 0 then 1 else d.natAbs / n.gcd d

