1. [THEOREM] Tangent-Cotangent Complementary Angle Identity: $\tan(\pi/2 - x) = \cot x$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic
Name: Real.tan_pi_div_two_sub
Description: For any real number $x$, the tangent of $\frac{\pi}{2} - x$ equals the reciprocal of the tangent of $x$, i.e., $\tan\left(\frac{\pi}{2} - x\right) = (\tan x)^{-1}$.
Signature:  (x : ℝ) : tan (π / 2 - x) = (tan x)⁻¹

2. [THEOREM] Numerator of Natural Number Cast to Rationals Equals Original Number
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs
Name: Rat.num_natCast
Description: For any natural number $n$, the numerator of the rational number corresponding to $n$ is equal to $n$ itself.
Signature:  (n : ℕ) : num n = n

3. [THEOREM] Sine Addition Identity: $\sin x + \sin y = 2 \sin\left(\frac{x + y}{2}\right) \cos\left(\frac{x - y}{2}\right)$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Complex.Trigonometric
Name: Complex.sin_add_sin
Description: For any complex numbers $x$ and $y$, the sum of sine functions satisfies the identity:
\[ \sin x + \sin y = 2 \sin\left(\frac{x + y}{2}\right) \cos\left(\frac{x - y}{2}\right). \]
Signature:  : sin x + sin y = 2 * sin ((x + y) / 2) * cos ((x - y) / 2)

4. [THEOREM] Sine of $(nπ - x)$ Identity: $\sin(nπ - x) = -(-1)^n \sin x$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic
Name: Real.sin_nat_mul_pi_sub
Description: For any real number $x$ and natural number $n$, the sine of $(n \pi - x)$ equals $-(-1)^n \sin x$.
Signature:  (x : ℝ) (n : ℕ) : sin (n * π - x) = -((-1) ^ n * sin x)

5. [THEOREM] Cotangent Identity: $\cot x = \frac{\cos x}{\sin x}$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Complex.Trigonometric
Name: Real.cot_eq_cos_div_sin
Description: For any real number $x$ where $\sin x \neq 0$, the cotangent of $x$ equals the ratio of the cosine of $x$ to the sine of $x$, i.e.,
\[ \cot x = \frac{\cos x}{\sin x}. \]
Signature:  : cot x = cos x / sin x

