3. [DEFINITION] Generalized Perron (GP) integration parameters
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.BoxIntegral.Partition.Filter
Name: BoxIntegral.IntegrationParams.GP
Description: The integration parameters for the generalized Perron (GP) integral, which is the least restrictive setting among the defined integration theories. These parameters require:
- The partition to be subordinate to a (possibly discontinuous) positive function $r$ (`bRiemann = false`),
- Each tag to belong to its corresponding closed box (`bHenstock = true`),
- An upper bound on the distortion (maximal side ratio) of all boxes in the partition (`bDistortion = true`).

This setting allows integration of a broader class of functions, including those where the divergence theorem holds without additional integrability assumptions.
