4. $g(a-1) \geq 0$.

Then the integral of $f(x)g(x-1)$ over $[a, b]$ is bounded above by the sum of the products $f(i)g(i)$ over integer points $i$ in the interval $[a, b)$, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x)g(x-1) \, dx \leq \sum_{i \in [a, b) \cap \mathbb{Z}} f(i)g(i). \]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : AntitoneOn f (Icc a b)) (hg : MonotoneOn g (Icc (a - 1) (b - 1))) (fpos : 0 ≤ f b)
  (gpos : 0 ≤ g (a - 1)) : ∫ x in a..b, f x * g (x - 1) ≤ ∑ i ∈ Finset.Ico a b, f i * g i
