1. [THEOREM] Upper Bound for Integral over Countable Union of Sets
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Lebesgue
Name: MeasureTheory.lintegral_iUnion_le
Description: For any countable family of sets $(s_i)_{i \in \beta}$ in a measurable space $\alpha$ and any measurable function $f \colon \alpha \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\infty\}$, the integral of $f$ over the union $\bigcup_i s_i$ with respect to measure $\mu$ is bounded above by the sum of integrals over each $s_i$:
\[
\int⁻_{a \in \bigcup_i s_i} f(a) \, d\mu \leq \sum_{i} \int⁻_{a \in s_i} f(a) \, d\mu.
\]
Signature:  [Countable β] (s : β → Set α) (f : α → ℝ≥0∞) : ∫⁻ a in ⋃ i, s i, f a ∂μ ≤ ∑' i, ∫⁻ a in s i, f a ∂μ

