4. [THEOREM] Monotonicity of Lebesgue Integral for Simple Functions with Respect to Measure
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.SimpleFunc
Name: MeasureTheory.SimpleFunc.lintegral_mono_measure
Description: For any simple function $f \colon \alpha \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\infty\}$ and measures $\mu, \nu$ on $\alpha$ such that $\mu \leq \nu$, the Lebesgue integral of $f$ with respect to $\mu$ is less than or equal to its integral with respect to $\nu$. That is:
\[
\int f \, d\mu \leq \int f \, d\nu.
\]
