<justification>
The function \(f(x)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{x}}\) is decreasing on \([1,10000]\); this is expressed by the hypothesis `h_antitone`.  
For a decreasing function, the right‑endpoint Riemann sum over the uniform partition  
\([1,2], [2,3],\dots,[9999,10000]\) is less than or equal to the integral over the whole interval:
\[
\sum_{i=1}^{9999} f(i+1)\cdot 1 \;\le\; \int_{1}^{10000} f(x)\,dx .
\]
In Lean this sum is written as  
`∑ i in Finset.Ico (1 : ℕ) 10000, (1 : ℝ) / Real.sqrt ((i : ℝ) + 1)`,  
and the integral as  
`∫ x in (1 : ℝ)..10000, (1 : ℝ) / Real.sqrt x`.  
Hence the inequality stated in the theorem follows directly from the monotonicity hypothesis, so the theorem is mathematically correct. No correction is needed.
</justification>
