3. [THEOREM] Lower bound for integral of products of antitone and monotone functions via sum
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons
Name: integral_le_sum_mul_Ico_of_antitone_monotone
Description: Let $a, b \in \mathbb{R}$ with $a \leq b$, and let $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ and $g \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be functions. Suppose that:
1. $f$ is antitone on the interval $[a, b]$,
2. $g$ is monotone on the interval $[a-1, b-1]$,
3. $f(b) \geq 0$,
4. $g(a-1) \geq 0$.

Then the integral of $f(x)g(x-1)$ over $[a, b]$ is bounded above by the sum of the products $f(i)g(i)$ over integer points $i$ in the interval $[a, b)$, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x)g(x-1) \, dx \leq \sum_{i \in [a, b) \cap \mathbb{Z}} f(i)g(i). \]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : AntitoneOn f (Icc a b)) (hg : MonotoneOn g (Icc (a - 1) (b - 1))) (fpos : 0 ≤ f b)
  (gpos : 0 ≤ g (a - 1)) : ∫ x in a..b, f x * g (x - 1) ≤ ∑ i ∈ Finset.Ico a b, f i * g i

4. [THEOREM] Upper bound for sum of products of monotone and antitone functions via integral
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons
Name: sum_mul_Ico_le_integral_of_monotone_antitone
Description: Let $a, b \in \mathbb{R}$ with $a \leq b$, and let $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ and $g \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be functions. Suppose that:
1. $f$ is monotone on the interval $[a, b]$,
2. $g$ is antitone on the interval $[a-1, b-1]$,
3. $f(a) \geq 0$,
4. $g(b-1) \geq 0$.

Then the sum of the products $f(i)g(i)$ over integer points $i$ in the interval $[a, b)$ is bounded above by the integral of $f(x)g(x-1)$ over $[a, b]$, i.e.,
\[ \sum_{i \in [a, b) \cap \mathbb{Z}} f(i)g(i) \leq \int_{a}^{b} f(x)g(x-1) \, dx. \]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : MonotoneOn f (Icc a b)) (hg : AntitoneOn g (Icc (a - 1) (b - 1))) (fpos : 0 ≤ f a)
  (gpos : 0 ≤ g (b - 1)) : ∑ i ∈ Finset.Ico a b, f i * g i ≤ ∫ x in a..b, f x * g (x - 1)

