1. [THEOREM] Membership of Right Endpoint in Open-Closed Interval: $b \in (a, b] \leftrightarrow a < b$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.right_mem_Ioc
Description: For elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$, the element $b$ belongs to the open-closed interval $(a, b]$ if and only if $a < b$.
Signature:  : b ∈ Ioc a b ↔ a < b

2. [THEOREM] Right Endpoint Membership in Closed Interval: $b \in [a, b] \leftrightarrow a \leq b$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.right_mem_Icc
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$, the element $b$ belongs to the closed interval $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ if and only if $a \leq b$.
Signature:  : b ∈ Icc a b ↔ a ≤ b

3. [THEOREM] Finset of Elements Below Top Equals Universal Finset in Finite Order with Top
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Iic_top
Description: In a locally finite order $\alpha$ with a greatest element $\top$ and where $\alpha$ is finite, the finset of elements less than or equal to $\top$ is equal to the entire finset of $\alpha$, i.e., $\text{Iic}(\top) = \text{univ}$.
Signature:  [OrderTop α] [Fintype α] : Iic (⊤ : α) = univ

4. [THEOREM] Left Endpoint Membership in Closed Interval
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.left_mem_Icc
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$, the element $a$ belongs to the closed interval $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ if and only if $a \leq b$.
Signature:  : a ∈ Icc a b ↔ a ≤ b

5. [THEOREM] Empty Closed Interval Finset When Reversed Order: $\text{Icc}(a, b) = \emptyset$ when $b < a$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Icc_eq_empty_of_lt
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$, if $b < a$, then the closed interval finset $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ is empty.
Signature:  (h : b < a) : Icc a b = ∅
