1. [THEOREM] Monotone Function Integral Bounded by Right-Endpoint Sum: $\int_a^b f \leq \sum_{i \in [a,b)} f(i+1)$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons
Name: MonotoneOn.integral_le_sum_Ico
Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be a function that is monotone (increasing) on the closed interval $[a, b]$, where $a \leq b$. Then the integral of $f$ over $[a, b]$ is bounded above by the sum of the values of $f$ at the right endpoints of the integer subintervals in $[a, b)$, i.e.,
\[
\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, dx \leq \sum_{i \in [a, b) \cap \mathbb{Z}} f(i+1).
\]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : MonotoneOn f (Set.Icc a b)) : (∫ x in a..b, f x) ≤ ∑ i ∈ Finset.Ico a b, f (i + 1 : ℕ)

2. [THEOREM] Sum of Monotone Function at Integer Points is Bounded by Integral over Interval
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons
Name: MonotoneOn.sum_le_integral_Ico
Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be a monotone (increasing) function on the closed interval $[a, b]$, where $a \leq b$. Then the sum of $f$ evaluated at the integer points in the half-open interval $[a, b)$ is bounded above by the integral of $f$ over $[a, b]$, i.e.,
\[
\sum_{x \in [a, b) \cap \mathbb{Z}} f(x) \leq \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, dx.
\]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : MonotoneOn f (Set.Icc a b)) : ∑ x ∈ Finset.Ico a b, f x ≤ ∫ x in a..b, f x

3. [THEOREM] Integral of Monotone Function is Bounded by Sum at Right Endpoints
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons
Name: MonotoneOn.integral_le_sum
Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be a function that is monotone (increasing) on the interval $[x_0, x_0 + a]$. Then the integral of $f$ over $[x_0, x_0 + a]$ is bounded above by the sum of the values of $f$ at the points $x_0 + (i + 1)$ for $i$ from $0$ to $a-1$, i.e.,
\[
\int_{x_0}^{x_0 + a} f(x) \, dx \leq \sum_{i=0}^{a-1} f(x_0 + i + 1).
\]
Signature:  (hf : MonotoneOn f (Icc x₀ (x₀ + a))) : (∫ x in x₀..x₀ + a, f x) ≤ ∑ i ∈ Finset.range a, f (x₀ + (i + 1 : ℕ))

4. [THEOREM] Sum of Monotone Function Values at Integer Points is Bounded by Integral
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons
Name: MonotoneOn.sum_le_integral
Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be a monotone (increasing) function on the interval $[x_0, x_0 + a]$. Then the sum of $f$ evaluated at the integer points $x_0, x_0 + 1, \ldots, x_0 + (a - 1)$ is bounded above by the integral of $f$ over $[x_0, x_0 + a]$, i.e.,
