4. [THEOREM] Integral Representation of L-series for Nonnegative Sequences with $O(n^r)$ Partial Sums
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.LSeries.SumCoeff
Name: LSeries_eq_mul_integral_of_nonneg
Description: Let $f \colon \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{R}$ be a sequence of nonnegative real numbers and $s \in \mathbb{C}$ with $\operatorname{Re}(s) > r \geq 0$. Suppose the partial sums $\sum_{k=1}^n f(k)$ are $O(n^r)$ as $n \to \infty$. Then the L-series $L(f, s)$ can be expressed as:
\[
L(f, s) = s \int_{t > 1} \left( \sum_{k=1}^{\lfloor t \rfloor} f(k) \right) t^{-(s+1)} \, dt.
\]
