Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: AntitoneOn.intervalIntegrable
Description: Let $u : \mathbb{R} \to E$ be a function that is antitone (i.e., decreasing) on the interval $[\min(a, b), \max(a, b)]$. Then $u$ is interval integrable on $[a, b]$ with respect to any measure $\mu$, meaning it is integrable on both $(a, b]$ and $(b, a]$.
