Signature:  (f : ℝ → E) (a b) : (∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ) ∈ ({∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ, -∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ} : Set E)

2. [DEFINITION] Interval integral of a function between two points
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: term∫_In_.._,_.delab_app.intervalIntegral
Description: The interval integral $\int_{x \in a..b} f(x) \, d\mu$ is defined as the difference $\int_{x \in \text{Ioc}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu - \int_{x \in \text{Ioc}(b,a)} f(x) \, d\mu$, where $\text{Ioc}(a,b)$ denotes the half-open interval $(a,b]$. When $a \leq b$, this equals $\int_{x \in \text{Ioc}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu$, and when $b \leq a$, it equals $-\int_{x \in \text{Ioc}(b,a)} f(x) \, d\mu$.
Signature:  : Delab✝

3. [THEOREM] Interval Integral Equals Scaled Integral Over Union Interval: $\int_a^b f = \pm \int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.intervalIntegral_eq_integral_uIoc
Description: For any real numbers $a$ and $b$ and any measurable function $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$, the interval integral $\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu$ equals the integral of $f$ over the interval $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b)]$, scaled by $1$ if $a \leq b$ and by $-1$ otherwise. That is,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu = \begin{cases}
\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu & \text{if } a \leq b \\
-\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases} \]
Signature:  (f : ℝ → E) (a b : ℝ) (μ : Measure ℝ) : ∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ = (if a ≤ b then 1 else -1 : ℝ) • ∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ

4. [THEOREM] Absolute Value Equality for Interval Integrals: $\left|\int_a^b f\right| = \left|\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f\right|$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.abs_intervalIntegral_eq
Description: For any real-valued function $f$ and real numbers $a, b$, the absolute value of the interval integral $\left|\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu\right|$ is equal to the absolute value of the integral of $f$ over the interval $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b)]$, i.e.,
\[ \left|\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu\right| = \left|\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu\right|. \]
Signature:  (f : ℝ → ℝ) (a b : ℝ) (μ : Measure ℝ) : |∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ| = |∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ|

