5. [THEOREM] Measure Inequality: $\limsup \mu_i(E^c) \leq \mu(E^c)$ implies $\mu(E) \leq \liminf \mu_i(E)$ for probability measures
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Portmanteau
Name: MeasureTheory.le_measure_liminf_of_limsup_measure_compl_le
Description: Let $\Omega$ be a measurable space, $\mu$ a probability measure on $\Omega$, and $(\mu_i)_{i\in\iota}$ a sequence of probability measures on $\Omega$. For any measurable set $E \subseteq \Omega$, if the limsup of the measures $\mu_i(E^c)$ is bounded above by $\mu(E^c)$, then the measure of $E$ under $\mu$ is bounded below by the liminf of the measures $\mu_i(E)$. In other words:

If $\limsup_{i} \mu_i(E^c) \leq \mu(E^c)$, then $\mu(E) \leq \liminf_{i} \mu_i(E)$.
