1. [THEOREM] Monotonicity of interval integral under almost everywhere inequality
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_mono_ae
Description: Let $f$ and $g$ be measurable functions on $\mathbb{R}$ with respect to a measure $\mu$. If $f \leq g$ holds almost everywhere with respect to $\mu$, then for any real numbers $a$ and $b$, the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ is less than or equal to the interval integral of $g$ from $a$ to $b$, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(u) \, d\mu \leq \int_{a}^{b} g(u) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  (h : f ≤ᵐ[μ] g) : (∫ u in a..b, f u ∂μ) ≤ ∫ u in a..b, g u ∂μ

2. [THEOREM] Positivity of Integral for Positive Functions on Open Interval
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.intervalIntegral_pos_of_pos_on
Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be an interval integrable function with respect to the Lebesgue measure on $[a,b]$. If $f$ is strictly positive on the open interval $(a,b)$ and $a < b$, then the integral $\int_a^b f(x) \, dx$ is strictly positive.
Signature:  {f : ℝ → ℝ} {a b : ℝ} (hfi : IntervalIntegrable f volume a b) (hpos : ∀ x : ℝ, x ∈ Ioo a b → 0 < f x) (hab : a < b) :
  0 < ∫ x : ℝ in a..b, f x

3. [THEOREM] Interval Integrability of Antitone Functions on $[a, b]$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: AntitoneOn.intervalIntegrable
Description: Let $u : \mathbb{R} \to E$ be a function that is antitone (i.e., decreasing) on the interval $[\min(a, b), \max(a, b)]$. Then $u$ is interval integrable on $[a, b]$ with respect to any measure $\mu$, meaning it is integrable on both $(a, b]$ and $(b, a]$.
Signature:  {u : ℝ → E} {a b : ℝ} (hu : AntitoneOn u (uIcc a b)) : IntervalIntegrable u μ a b
