2. [THEOREM] Nonnegativity of Interval Integral on $[a,b]$ for Nonnegative Functions
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_nonneg
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$ and any function $f$, if $f(u) \geq 0$ for all $u$ in the closed interval $[a, b]$, then the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ is nonnegative, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(u) \, d\mu \geq 0. \]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : ∀ u, u ∈ Icc a b → 0 ≤ f u) : 0 ≤ ∫ u in a..b, f u ∂μ

3. [THEOREM] Interval Integrability of Antitone Functions on $[a, b]$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: AntitoneOn.intervalIntegrable
Description: Let $u : \mathbb{R} \to E$ be a function that is antitone (i.e., decreasing) on the interval $[\min(a, b), \max(a, b)]$. Then $u$ is interval integrable on $[a, b]$ with respect to any measure $\mu$, meaning it is integrable on both $(a, b]$ and $(b, a]$.
Signature:  {u : ℝ → E} {a b : ℝ} (hu : AntitoneOn u (uIcc a b)) : IntervalIntegrable u μ a b
