Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.FundThmCalculus
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt
Description: Let $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$ be a function such that for every $x$ in the closed interval $\text{uIcc}(a, b)$ (the smallest interval containing $a$ and $b$), $f$ has a derivative $f'(x)$ at $x$, and $f'$ is integrable on $[a, b]$. Then:
