8. [THEOREM] Sum of Centroid Weight Indicators Equals Sum of Centroid Weights
Module: Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.AffineSpace.Combination
Name: Finset.sum_centroidWeightsIndicator
Description: For a finite type $\iota$ and a finite subset $s \subseteq \iota$, the sum of the centroid weight indicators over all indices $i \in \iota$ equals the sum of the centroid weights over the indices $i \in s$. That is,
\[ \sum_{i \in \iota} w_i = \sum_{i \in s} w_i, \]
where $w_i$ is the centroid weight indicator function, which assigns $(|s|)^{-1}$ to each $i \in s$ and $0$ otherwise.
Signature:  [Fintype ι] : ∑ i, s.centroidWeightsIndicator k i = ∑ i ∈ s, s.centroidWeights k i
