Module: Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic
Name: antitone_const
Description: For any constant function $f \colon \alpha \to \beta$ between two preorders, where $f(x) = c$ for some fixed $c \in \beta$, the function $f$ is antitone. That is, for all $a, b \in \alpha$, if $a \leq b$, then $c \leq c$.
Signature:  [Preorder α] [Preorder β] {c : β} : Antitone fun _ : α ↦ c

5. [THEOREM] Strictly Antitone Functions are Antitone
Module: Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic
Name: StrictAntiOn.antitoneOn
Description: If a function $f \colon \alpha \to \beta$ is strictly antitone on a set $s \subseteq \alpha$, then it is also antitone on $s$. That is, for all $a, b \in s$, if $a < b$ implies $f(b) < f(a)$, then $a \leq b$ implies $f(b) \leq f(a)$.
Signature:  (hf : StrictAntiOn f s) : AntitoneOn f s
