1. [THEOREM] Empty Closed Interval Finset Criterion: $\text{Icc}(a, b) = \emptyset \leftrightarrow a \nleq b$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Icc_eq_empty_iff
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a preorder $\alpha$, the finset $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ is empty if and only if $a$ is not less than or equal to $b$, i.e., $\text{Icc}(a, b) = \emptyset \leftrightarrow \neg (a \leq b)$.
Signature:  : Icc a b = ∅ ↔ ¬a ≤ b

2. [THEOREM] Right Endpoint Membership in Closed Interval: $b \in [a, b] \leftrightarrow a \leq b$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.right_mem_Icc
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$, the element $b$ belongs to the closed interval $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ if and only if $a \leq b$.
Signature:  : b ∈ Icc a b ↔ a ≤ b

3. [THEOREM] Inclusion Condition for Closed Finset Interval in Closed-Open Finset Interval: $\text{Icc}(a₁, b₁) \subseteq \text{Ico}(a₂, b₂) \leftrightarrow a₂ \leq a₁ \land b₁ < b₂$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Icc_subset_Ico_iff
Description: For any elements $a₁, b₁, a₂, b₂$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$ with $a₁ \leq b₁$, the finset $\text{Icc}(a₁, b₁)$ is a subset of the finset $\text{Ico}(a₂, b₂)$ if and only if $a₂ \leq a₁$ and $b₁ < b₂$.
Signature:  (h₁ : a₁ ≤ b₁) : Icc a₁ b₁ ⊆ Ico a₂ b₂ ↔ a₂ ≤ a₁ ∧ b₁ < b₂

