2. [THEOREM] Inclusion Condition for Closed Finset Interval in Closed-Open Finset Interval: $\text{Icc}(a₁, b₁) \subseteq \text{Ico}(a₂, b₂) \leftrightarrow a₂ \leq a₁ \land b₁ < b₂$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Icc_subset_Ico_iff
Description: For any elements $a₁, b₁, a₂, b₂$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$ with $a₁ \leq b₁$, the finset $\text{Icc}(a₁, b₁)$ is a subset of the finset $\text{Ico}(a₂, b₂)$ if and only if $a₂ \leq a₁$ and $b₁ < b₂$.
Signature:  (h₁ : a₁ ≤ b₁) : Icc a₁ b₁ ⊆ Ico a₂ b₂ ↔ a₂ ≤ a₁ ∧ b₁ < b₂

3. [THEOREM] Finset Coefficients of Closed Interval Equal Set Interval
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Defs
Name: Finset.coe_Icc
Description: For any elements $a, b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$, the underlying set of the finset $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ is equal to the closed interval $\{x \in \alpha \mid a \leq x \leq b\}$.
Signature:  (a b : α) : (Icc a b : Set α) = Set.Icc a b

4. [THEOREM] Difference of Closed and Closed-Open Interval Finsets: $\text{Icc}(a,b) \setminus \text{Ico}(a,b) = \{b\}$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Icc_diff_Ico_self
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$ with $a \leq b$, the set difference between the finsets $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ and $\text{Ico}(a, b)$ is the singleton finset $\{b\}$. In other words, $\text{Icc}(a, b) \setminus \text{Ico}(a, b) = \{b\}$.
Signature:  (h : a ≤ b) : Icc a b \ Ico a b = { b }

5. [THEOREM] Inserting Right Endpoint into Closed-Open Interval Yields Closed Interval: $\text{Ico}(a, b) \cup \{b\} = \text{Icc}(a, b)$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Ico_insert_right
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$ with $a \leq b$, inserting the right endpoint $b$ into the closed-open interval finset $[a, b)$ yields the closed interval finset $[a, b]$. That is, $\text{Ico}(a, b) \cup \{b\} = \text{Icc}(a, b)$.
Signature:  (h : a ≤ b) : insert b (Ico a b) = Icc a b

