Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be a monotone (increasing) function on the interval $[x_0, x_0 + a]$. Then the sum of $f$ evaluated at the integer points $x_0, x_0 + 1, \ldots, x_0 + (a - 1)$ is bounded above by the integral of $f$ over $[x_0, x_0 + a]$, i.e.,
\[
\sum_{i=0}^{a-1} f(x_0 + i) \leq \int_{x_0}^{x_0 + a} f(x) \, dx.
\]
Signature:  (hf : MonotoneOn f (Icc x₀ (x₀ + a))) : (∑ i ∈ Finset.range a, f (x₀ + i)) ≤ ∫ x in x₀..x₀ + a, f x

