\[ c \cdot \int_{a}^{b} f(x \cdot c) \, dx = \int_{a \cdot c}^{b \cdot c} f(x) \, dx. \]
Signature:  : (c * ∫ x in a..b, f (x * c)) = ∫ x in a * c..b * c, f x

3. [THEOREM] Change of Variables: \( c^{-1} \cdot \int_{a}^{b} f(x/c + d) \, dx = \int_{a/c + d}^{b/c + d} f(x) \, dx \)
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals
Name: intervalIntegral.inv_mul_integral_comp_div_add
Description: For any real numbers \( a, b, c \neq 0 \), and \( d \), and any integrable function \( f \), the following equality holds:
\[ c^{-1} \cdot \int_{a}^{b} f\left(\frac{x}{c} + d\right) \, dx = \int_{\frac{a}{c} + d}^{\frac{b}{c} + d} f(x) \, dx. \]
Signature:  : (c⁻¹ * ∫ x in a..b, f (x / c + d)) = ∫ x in a / c + d..b / c + d, f x

4. [THEOREM] Change of Variables Formula: \(\frac{1}{c} \int_{a}^{b} f(d - x/c) \, dx = \int_{d - b/c}^{d - a/c} f(x) \, dx\)
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals
Name: intervalIntegral.inv_mul_integral_comp_sub_div
Description: For any real numbers \( a, b, c, d \) with \( c \neq 0 \), and any integrable function \( f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R} \), the following equality holds:
