5. [DEFINITION] Four-way commutativity of sum types
Module: Mathlib.Logic.Equiv.Basic
Name: Equiv.sumSumSumComm
Description: The equivalence $(α ⊕ β) ⊕ (γ ⊕ δ) ≃ (α ⊕ γ) ⊕ (β ⊕ δ)$ demonstrates a four-way commutativity property of sum types, analogous to the commutativity of addition. The bijection is constructed through a composition of associativity and commutativity equivalences for sum types, with the following key steps:
1. First applies the inverse of associativity to $(α ⊕ β) ⊕ (γ ⊕ δ)$
2. Then swaps the middle components $β$ and $γ$ via commutativity
3. Finally reassociates to obtain $(α ⊕ γ) ⊕ (β ⊕ δ)$

The inverse function follows the reverse path. The equivalence is proved by case analysis showing both compositions yield identity maps.
