5. [DEFINITION] Interval integrability of a function
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: IntervalIntegrable
Description: A function $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$ is called *interval integrable* with respect to a measure $\mu$ on an interval from $a$ to $b$ if it is integrable on both intervals $(a, b]$ and $(b, a]$. Since one of these intervals is always empty, this is equivalent to $f$ being integrable on $(\min(a, b), \max(a, b)]$.
Signature:  (f : ℝ → E) (μ : Measure ℝ) (a b : ℝ) : Prop
