1. [THEOREM] Closed Interval Subset Criterion: $[a_1, b_1] \subseteq [a_2, b_2] \iff a_2 \leq a_1 \wedge b_1 \leq b_2$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Set.Basic
Name: Set.Icc_subset_Icc_iff
Description: For elements $a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2$ in a preorder $\alpha$ with $a_1 \leq b_1$, the closed interval $[a_1, b_1]$ is a subset of the closed interval $[a_2, b_2]$ if and only if $a_2 \leq a_1$ and $b_1 \leq b_2$.
Signature:  (h₁ : a₁ ≤ b₁) : Icc a₁ b₁ ⊆ Icc a₂ b₂ ↔ a₂ ≤ a₁ ∧ b₁ ≤ b₂

2. [THEOREM] Continuity of Division by a Constant: $f(x)/y$ is Continuous for Continuous $f$
Module: Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.GroupWithZero
Name: Continuous.div_const
Description: Let $G₀$ be a topological space with a division operation and continuous multiplication. For any continuous function $f \colon X \to G₀$ and any constant $y \in G₀$, the function $x \mapsto f(x) / y$ is continuous.
Signature:  (hf : Continuous f) (y : G₀) : Continuous fun x => f x / y

