2. [THEOREM] Integral of Constant Function: $\int_{a}^{b} c \, dx = (b - a)c$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_const
Description: Let $E$ be a complete space and $c \in E$ be a constant. The integral of the constant function $x \mapsto c$ over the interval $[a, b]$ with respect to the Lebesgue measure is given by:
