1. [THEOREM] Scaling and Translation Property of Interval Integral: $\int_{a}^{b} f(cx + d) \, dx = c^{-1} \int_{ca + d}^{cb + d} f(x) \, dx$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_comp_mul_add
Description: For any nonzero real number $c \neq 0$ and any real number $d$, the integral of the function $f(cx + d)$ over the interval $[a, b]$ equals $c^{-1}$ times the integral of $f(x)$ over the interval $[ca + d, cb + d]$. That is,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(cx + d) \, dx = c^{-1} \int_{ca + d}^{cb + d} f(x) \, dx. \]
