Name: intervalIntegral.integral_lt_integral_of_continuousOn_of_le_of_exists_lt
Description: Let $f, g \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be continuous functions on the closed interval $[a, b]$, with $a < b$. If $f(x) \leq g(x)$ for all $x \in (a, b]$ and there exists a point $c \in [a, b]$ such that $f(c) < g(c)$, then the integral of $f$ over $[a, b]$ is strictly less than the integral of $g$ over the same interval, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, dx < \int_{a}^{b} g(x) \, dx. \]
