1. [THEOREM] Constant Functions are Antitone on Any Subset
Module: Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic
Name: antitoneOn_const
Description: For any constant function $f \colon \alpha \to \beta$ between two preorders, where $f(x) = c$ for some fixed $c \in \beta$, and for any subset $s \subseteq \alpha$, the function $f$ is antitone on $s$. That is, for all $a, b \in s$, if $a \leq b$, then $c \leq c$.
Signature:  [Preorder α] [Preorder β] {c : β} {s : Set α} : AntitoneOn (fun _ : α ↦ c) s

2. [THEOREM] Positivity of Square Root: $\sqrt{x} > 0 \leftrightarrow x > 0$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_pos
Description: For any real number $x$, the square root of $x$ is positive if and only if $x$ is positive, i.e., $\sqrt{x} > 0 \leftrightarrow x > 0$.
Signature:  : 0 < √x ↔ 0 < x

3. [THEOREM] Inequality of One and Quotient: $1 < a/b \leftrightarrow b < a$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Group.Unbundled.Basic
Name: one_lt_div'
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in an ordered group, the inequality $1 < a / b$ holds if and only if $b < a$.
Signature:  : 1 < a / b ↔ b < a

