Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.StronglyMeasurable.AEStronglyMeasurable
Name: MeasureTheory.AEStronglyMeasurable.restrict
Description: Let $f \colon \alpha \to \beta$ be an almost everywhere strongly measurable function with respect to a measure $\mu$ on a measurable space $\alpha$. Then for any measurable set $s \subseteq \alpha$, the restriction of $f$ is also almost everywhere strongly measurable with respect to the restricted measure $\mu|_s$.
Signature:  (hfm : AEStronglyMeasurable[m] f μ) {s} : AEStronglyMeasurable[m] f (μ.restrict s)

2. [THEOREM] Almost Everywhere Strong Measurability Preservation under Measure Restriction
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.StronglyMeasurable.AEStronglyMeasurable
Name: MeasureTheory.AEStronglyMeasurable.of_trim
Description: Let $(α, m₀)$ be a measurable space with a measure $\mu$, and let $m₀' \leq m₀$ be a sub-$\sigma$-algebra. If a function $f \colon α \to β$ is almost everywhere strongly measurable with respect to $m$ and the restricted measure $\mu|_{m₀'}$, then $f$ is also almost everywhere strongly measurable with respect to $m$ and the original measure $\mu$.
Signature:  {m₀' : MeasurableSpace α} (hm₀ : m₀' ≤ m₀) (hf : AEStronglyMeasurable[m] f (μ.trim hm₀)) : AEStronglyMeasurable[m] f μ

3. [THEOREM] Almost Everywhere Membership of Measurable Set in Its Own Restricted Measure
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Restrict
Name: MeasureTheory.self_mem_ae_restrict
Description: For any measurable set $s$ in a measure space $(α, \mathcal{M}, μ)$, the set $s$ belongs to the almost everywhere filter of the restricted measure $\mu|_s$. In other words, $s$ contains almost every point with respect to the measure $\mu|_s$.
Signature:  {s} (hs : MeasurableSet s) : s ∈ ae (μ.restrict s)

4. [THEOREM] Measure restriction equals original measure when restricting to a full measure set
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Restrict
Name: MeasureTheory.Measure.restrict_eq_self_of_ae_mem
Description: Let $\mu$ be a measure on a measurable space $\alpha$ and let $s \subseteq \alpha$ be a subset such that $\mu$-almost every point $x$ belongs to $s$ (i.e., $\{x \notin s\}$ has $\mu$-measure zero). Then the restriction of $\mu$ to $s$ equals $\mu$ itself, i.e.,
\[ \mu|_s = \mu. \]
Signature:  {_m0 : MeasurableSpace α} ⦃s : Set α⦄ ⦃μ : Measure α⦄ (hs : ∀ᵐ x ∂μ, x ∈ s) : μ.restrict s = μ

