1. [DEFINITION] Generalized Perron (GP) integration parameters
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.BoxIntegral.Partition.Filter
Name: BoxIntegral.IntegrationParams.GP
Description: The integration parameters for the generalized Perron (GP) integral, which is the least restrictive setting among the defined integration theories. These parameters require:
- The partition to be subordinate to a (possibly discontinuous) positive function $r$ (`bRiemann = false`),
- Each tag to belong to its corresponding closed box (`bHenstock = true`),
- An upper bound on the distortion (maximal side ratio) of all boxes in the partition (`bDistortion = true`).

This setting allows integration of a broader class of functions, including those where the divergence theorem holds without additional integrability assumptions.
Signature:  : IntegrationParams

2. [THEOREM] Integral of Exponential Function: $\int_a^b e^x dx = e^b - e^a$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals
Name: integral_exp
Description: For any real numbers $a$ and $b$, the integral of the exponential function from $a$ to $b$ equals the difference of the exponential function evaluated at the endpoints, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} e^x \, dx = e^b - e^a. \]
Signature:  : ∫ x in a..b, exp x = exp b - exp a

3. [THEOREM] Scaled Integral Transformation: $c \cdot \int_{a}^{b} f(cx) \, dx = \int_{ac}^{bc} f(x) \, dx$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals
Name: intervalIntegral.mul_integral_comp_mul_right
Description: For any real number $c$ and any integrable function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$, the product $c \cdot \int_{a}^{b} f(x \cdot c) \, dx$ equals the integral of $f(x)$ over the interval $[a \cdot c, b \cdot c]$, i.e.,
