Name: MeasureTheory.ae_toFinite
Description: For any s-finite measure $\mu$ on a measurable space, the almost everywhere equality relation with respect to the finite measure $\mu_{\text{toFinite}}$ coincides with the almost everywhere equality relation with respect to $\mu$ itself, i.e., $\text{ae}(\mu_{\text{toFinite}}) = \text{ae}(\mu)$.
Signature:  [SFinite μ] : ae μ.toFinite = ae μ

4. [THEOREM] Almost Everywhere Equality of Auxiliary Finite Measure and Original S-Finite Measure
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.WithDensityFinite
Name: MeasureTheory.ae_toFiniteAux
Description: For any s-finite measure $\mu$, the almost everywhere equality relation with respect to the auxiliary finite measure $\mu_{\text{toFiniteAux}}$ coincides with the almost everywhere equality relation with respect to $\mu$ itself, i.e., $\text{ae}(\mu_{\text{toFiniteAux}}) = \text{ae}(\mu)$.
Signature:  [SFinite μ] : ae μ.toFiniteAux = ae μ

5. [THEOREM] Equality of Almost Everywhere Filters under Scalar Multiplication of Measures
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.MeasureSpace
Name: MeasureTheory.Measure.ae_smul_measure_eq
Description: For any nonzero scalar $c$ and measure $\mu$ on a measurable space $\alpha$, the almost everywhere filter of the scaled measure $c \cdot \mu$ is equal to the almost everywhere filter of $\mu$. That is, $\text{ae}(c \cdot \mu) = \text{ae}(\mu)$.
Signature:  (hc : c ≠ 0) (μ : Measure α) : ae (c • μ) = ae μ
