1. [THEOREM] Equality of Restricted Measures for Finite Measures
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.FiniteMeasure
Name: MeasureTheory.FiniteMeasure.restrict_measure_eq
Description: For any finite measure $\mu$ on a measurable space $\Omega$ and any measurable set $A \subseteq \Omega$, the underlying measure of the restriction $\mu|_A$ is equal to the restriction of the underlying measure of $\mu$ to $A$. That is, $(\mu|_A) = \mu|_A$ as measures.
Signature:  (μ : FiniteMeasure Ω) (A : Set Ω) : (μ.restrict A : Measure Ω) = (μ : Measure Ω).restrict A

2. [THEOREM] Equality of Linear Restriction Map and Measure Restriction
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Restrict
Name: MeasureTheory.Measure.restrictₗ_apply
Description: For any measurable space $\alpha$, subset $s \subseteq \alpha$, and measure $\mu$ on $\alpha$, the linear restriction map $\text{restrict}_{\text{ₗ}}$ applied to $s$ and $\mu$ equals the restriction of $\mu$ to $s$, i.e.,
\[
\text{restrict}_{\text{ₗ}} s \mu = \mu|_s.
\]
Signature:  {_m0 : MeasurableSpace α} (s : Set α) (μ : Measure α) : restrictₗ s μ = μ.restrict s

3. [THEOREM] Equality of Measure Restrictions on Open and Closed Left Rays for Atomless Measures
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Typeclasses
Name: MeasureTheory.restrict_Iio_eq_restrict_Iic
Description: For an atomless measure $\mu$ on a measurable space, the restriction of $\mu$ to the open left ray $(-\infty, a)$ is equal to the restriction of $\mu$ to the closed left ray $(-\infty, a]$.
Signature:  : μ.restrict (Iio a) = μ.restrict (Iic a)

4. [THEOREM] Restriction of Measure Difference Equals Difference of Restrictions
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Sub
Name: MeasureTheory.Measure.restrict_sub_eq_restrict_sub_restrict
Description: For any measurable set $s$ in a measurable space $\alpha$, the restriction of the measure difference $\mu - \nu$ to $s$ equals the difference of the restricted measures $\mu$ and $\nu$ to $s$. That is,
\[ (\mu - \nu)\restriction s = \mu\restriction s - \nu\restriction s. \]
Signature:  (h_meas_s : MeasurableSet s) : (μ - ν).restrict s = μ.restrict s - ν.restrict s

5. [THEOREM] Measure restriction equals original measure when restricting to a full measure set
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Restrict
Name: MeasureTheory.Measure.restrict_eq_self_of_ae_mem
Description: Let $\mu$ be a measure on a measurable space $\alpha$ and let $s \subseteq \alpha$ be a subset such that $\mu$-almost every point $x$ belongs to $s$ (i.e., $\{x \notin s\}$ has $\mu$-measure zero). Then the restriction of $\mu$ to $s$ equals $\mu$ itself, i.e.,
\[ \mu|_s = \mu. \]
Signature:  {_m0 : MeasurableSpace α} ⦃s : Set α⦄ ⦃μ : Measure α⦄ (hs : ∀ᵐ x ∂μ, x ∈ s) : μ.restrict s = μ
Results for query: eventually_of_forall tactic / lemma
1. [THEOREM] Universally True Predicate is Eventually True in Any Filter
Module: Mathlib.Order.Filter.Basic
Name: Filter.Eventually.of_forall
Description: For any filter $f$ on a type $\alpha$ and a predicate $p : \alpha \to \text{Prop}$, if $p(x)$ holds for all $x \in \alpha$, then $p$ holds eventually with respect to $f$ (i.e., $\forallᶠ x \text{ in } f, p\ x$).
Signature:  {p : α → Prop} {f : Filter α} (hp : ∀ x, p x) : ∀ᶠ x in f, p x

2. [THEOREM] Universal Quantifier Commutation with Eventually in Filters
Module: Mathlib.Order.Filter.Basic
Name: Filter.forall_eventually_of_eventually_forall
Description: For any filter $f$ on a type $\alpha$ and any predicate $p : \alpha \to \beta \to \text{Prop}$, if for eventually all $x$ in $f$ the property $p(x, y)$ holds for all $y \in \beta$, then for every $y \in \beta$, the property $p(x, y)$ holds for eventually all $x$ in $f$.

In notation:
\[
(\forallᶠ x \text{ in } f, \forall y, p(x, y)) \implies (\forall y, \forallᶠ x \text{ in } f, p(x, y))
\]
Signature:  {f : Filter α} {p : α → β → Prop} (h : ∀ᶠ x in f, ∀ y, p x y) : ∀ y, ∀ᶠ x in f, p x y

3. [THEOREM] Local Truth of Predicate in Neighborhood Within Set
Module: Mathlib.Topology.ContinuousOn
Name: eventually_nhdsWithin_of_forall
Description: For any subset $s$ of a type $\alpha$, any point $a \in \alpha$, and any predicate $p : \alpha \to \text{Prop}$, if $p(x)$ holds for all $x \in s$, then $p(x)$ holds for all $x$ in some neighborhood of $a$ within $s$ (i.e., $p$ holds eventually in the filter $\mathcal{N}_s(a)$).
Signature:  {s : Set α} {a : α} {p : α → Prop} (h : ∀ x ∈ s, p x) : ∀ᶠ x in 𝓝[s] a, p x

4. [THEOREM] Characterization of Eventually True Properties in the At-Top Filter
Module: Mathlib.Order.Filter.AtTopBot
Name: Filter.eventually_atTop
Description: A property $p$ holds eventually for the filter `atTop` (i.e., for all sufficiently large elements) if and only if there exists an element $a$ in the preordered type $\alpha$ such that for all $b \geq a$, the property $p(b)$ holds.
Signature:  : (∀ᶠ x in atTop, p x) ↔ ∃ a, ∀ b ≥ a, p b

5. [THEOREM] Eventual Universal Quantification under Tendency to Infinity
Module: Mathlib.Order.Filter.AtTopBot
Name: Filter.Tendsto.eventually_forall_ge_atTop
Description: Let $\beta$ be a preorder, $l$ a filter on a type $\alpha$, and $p : \beta \to \text{Prop}$ a predicate. If a function $f : \alpha \to \beta$ tends to infinity in $l$ (i.e., $\text{Tendsto}\,f\,l\,\text{atTop}$) and $p(x)$ holds for all sufficiently large $x$ in $\text{atTop}$, then for all sufficiently large $x$ in $l$, $p(y)$ holds for every $y \geq f(x)$.
Signature:  [Preorder β] {l : Filter α} {p : β → Prop} {f : α → β} (hf : Tendsto f l atTop) (h_evtl : ∀ᶠ x in atTop, p x) :
  ∀ᶠ x in l, ∀ y, f x ≤ y → p y
