1. [THEOREM] Bochner Integral of a Constant Function
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Bochner
Name: MeasureTheory.integral_const
Description: For any constant function $f(x) = c$ where $c$ is an element of a Banach space $E$, the Bochner integral of $f$ with respect to a measure $\mu$ on a space $\alpha$ is equal to the scalar multiplication of $c$ by the total measure of $\alpha$, i.e.,
\[ \int_\alpha c \, d\mu = \mu(\alpha)_{\text{toReal}} \cdot c. \]
Here, $\mu(\alpha)_{\text{toReal}}$ denotes the real-valued conversion of the measure of the entire space $\alpha$.
Signature:  (c : E) : ∫ _ : α, c ∂μ = (μ univ).toReal • c

