2. [THEOREM] Measure Zero Characterization via Almost Everywhere Non-Membership
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.OuterMeasure.AE
Name: MeasureTheory.measure_zero_iff_ae_nmem
Description: For any subset $s$ of a type $\alpha$ and a measure $\mu$ on $\alpha$, the measure of $s$ is zero if and only if $\mu$-almost every element $a$ does not belong to $s$. In other words, $\mu(s) = 0 \leftrightarrow \forall a \ \mu\text{-a.e.}, a \notin s$.
