1. [THEOREM] Restriction of a Function Equals Composition with Inclusion
Module: Mathlib.Data.Set.Function
Name: Set.restrict_eq
Description: For any function $f \colon \alpha \to \beta$ and any subset $s \subseteq \alpha$, the restriction of $f$ to $s$ is equal to the composition of $f$ with the canonical inclusion map from $s$ to $\alpha$. That is, $\text{restrict}_s f = f \circ \text{val}$, where $\text{val} \colon s \to \alpha$ is the inclusion map sending each element of $s$ to itself in $\alpha$.
Signature:  (f : α → β) (s : Set α) : s.restrict f = f ∘ Subtype.val

2. [THEOREM] Almost Everywhere Property on Union of Sets Equals Conjunction of Component Properties
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Restrict
Name: MeasureTheory.ae_restrict_union_iff
Description: For any subsets $s$ and $t$ of a measurable space $\alpha$ and any property $p : \alpha \to \text{Prop}$, the property $p$ holds $\mu$-almost everywhere on the restriction of $\mu$ to $s \cup t$ if and only if $p$ holds $\mu$-almost everywhere on both $\mu|_s$ and $\mu|_t$. 

In other words:
\[ \left(\forall^\mu x \in s \cup t, p(x)\right) \leftrightarrow \left(\forall^\mu x \in s, p(x)\right) \land \left(\forall^\mu x \in t, p(x)\right) \]
Signature:  (s t : Set α) (p : α → Prop) : (∀ᵐ x ∂μ.restrict (s ∪ t), p x) ↔ (∀ᵐ x ∂μ.restrict s, p x) ∧ ∀ᵐ x ∂μ.restrict t, p x

3. [THEOREM] Composition of Nested Restrictions: $(\text{restrict}_s^t) \circ (\text{restrict}_t^u) = \text{restrict}_s^u$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Set.Function
Name: Set.restrict₂_comp_restrict₂
Description: For any nested subsets $s \subseteq t \subseteq u$ of a type $\alpha$, the composition of the restriction from $t$ to $s$ with the restriction from $u$ to $t$ is equal to the restriction from $u$ to $s$. That is, for any function $f$ defined on $u$, we have:
\[ (\text{restrict}_s^t) \circ (\text{restrict}_t^u) = \text{restrict}_s^u \]
where $\text{restrict}_A^B$ denotes the restriction of a function from set $B$ to set $A$.
Signature:  {s t u : Set α} (hst : s ⊆ t) (htu : t ⊆ u) : (restrict₂ (π := π) hst) ∘ (restrict₂ htu) = restrict₂ (hst.trans htu)

4. [THEOREM] Almost Everywhere Filter Equality for Finite Union of Measure Restrictions
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Restrict
Name: MeasureTheory.ae_restrict_biUnion_finset_eq
Description: For a family of subsets $\{s_i\}_{i \in \iota}$ of a measurable space $\alpha$ and a finite set $t \subseteq \iota$, the almost everywhere filter of the measure $\mu$ restricted to the finite union $\bigcup_{i \in t} s_i$ equals the supremum of the almost everywhere filters of $\mu$ restricted to each $s_i$ for $i \in t$. That is:
\[ \text{ae}(\mu|_{\bigcup_{i \in t} s_i}) = \bigsqcup_{i \in t} \text{ae}(\mu|_{s_i}) \]
Signature:  (s : ι → Set α) (t : Finset ι) : ae (μ.restrict (⋃ i ∈ t, s i)) = ⨆ i ∈ t, ae (μ.restrict (s i))

