2. [THEOREM] Nonnegativity of Interval Integral Under Almost Everywhere Nonnegative Condition
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_nonneg_of_ae
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$ and any measurable function $f$ with respect to a measure $\mu$, if $f$ is almost everywhere nonnegative (i.e., $0 \leq f(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x \in \mathbb{R}$), then the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ is nonnegative, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu \geq 0. \]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : 0 ≤ᵐ[μ] f) : 0 ≤ ∫ u in a..b, f u ∂μ

