1. [THEOREM] Interval Integrability of the Identity Function
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals
Name: intervalIntegral.intervalIntegrable_id
Description: The identity function $f(x) = x$ is interval integrable on any interval $[a, b]$ with respect to any measure $\mu$.
Signature:  : IntervalIntegrable (fun x => x) μ a b

2. [THEOREM] Monotonicity of Interval Integral under Pointwise Inequality on $[a,b]$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_mono_on
Description: For any real numbers $a$ and $b$, and measurable functions $f, g : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$, if $f(x) \leq g(x)$ for all $x$ in the closed interval $[a, b]$, then the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ is less than or equal to the interval integral of $g$ from $a$ to $b$, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(u) \, d\mu \leq \int_{a}^{b} g(u) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  (h : ∀ x ∈ Icc a b, f x ≤ g x) : (∫ u in a..b, f u ∂μ) ≤ ∫ u in a..b, g u ∂μ

