2. [THEOREM] Norm of integral bounded by integral of norm over ordered interval
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.norm_integral_le_integral_norm
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$ and any function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$, the norm of the integral of $f$ over the interval $[a, b]$ is bounded above by the integral of the norm of $f$ over the same interval. That is,
\[ \left\| \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu \right\| \leq \int_{a}^{b} \|f(x)\| \, d\mu. \]
