Description: If a function $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$ is integrable with respect to a measure $\mu$ on $\mathbb{R}$, then $f$ is interval integrable with respect to $\mu$ on any interval $[a, b]$, i.e., $f$ is integrable on both $(a, b]$ and $(b, a]$.
Signature:  (hf : Integrable f μ) : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b

