1. [THEOREM] Constant Functions are Antitone on Any Subset
Module: Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic
Name: antitoneOn_const
Description: For any constant function $f \colon \alpha \to \beta$ between two preorders, where $f(x) = c$ for some fixed $c \in \beta$, and for any subset $s \subseteq \alpha$, the function $f$ is antitone on $s$. That is, for all $a, b \in s$, if $a \leq b$, then $c \leq c$.
Signature:  [Preorder α] [Preorder β] {c : β} {s : Set α} : AntitoneOn (fun _ : α ↦ c) s

2. [THEOREM] Absolute Value Equality for Interval Integrals: $\left|\int_a^b f\right| = \left|\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f\right|$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.abs_intervalIntegral_eq
Description: For any real-valued function $f$ and real numbers $a, b$, the absolute value of the interval integral $\left|\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu\right|$ is equal to the absolute value of the integral of $f$ over the interval $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b)]$, i.e.,
\[ \left|\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu\right| = \left|\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu\right|. \]
Signature:  (f : ℝ → ℝ) (a b : ℝ) (μ : Measure ℝ) : |∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ| = |∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ|

3. [THEOREM] Constant Functions are Antitone
Module: Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic
Name: antitone_const
Description: For any constant function $f \colon \alpha \to \beta$ between two preorders, where $f(x) = c$ for some fixed $c \in \beta$, the function $f$ is antitone. That is, for all $a, b \in \alpha$, if $a \leq b$, then $c \leq c$.
Signature:  [Preorder α] [Preorder β] {c : β} : Antitone fun _ : α ↦ c

4. [THEOREM] Scaling Property of Interval Integral: $\int_{a}^{b} f(cx) \, dx = c^{-1} \int_{ca}^{cb} f(x) \, dx$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_comp_mul_left
Description: For any nonzero real number $c \neq 0$ and any integrable function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$, the integral of $f(c \cdot x)$ over the interval $[a, b]$ is equal to $c^{-1}$ times the integral of $f(x)$ over the scaled interval $[c \cdot a, c \cdot b]$. That is,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(c \cdot x) \, dx = c^{-1} \cdot \int_{c \cdot a}^{c \cdot b} f(x) \, dx. \]
Signature:  (hc : c ≠ 0) : (∫ x in a..b, f (c * x)) = c⁻¹ • ∫ x in c * a..c * b, f x

5. [THEOREM] Possible Values of Interval Integral: $\int_a^b f \in \{\pm \int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f\}$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_cases
Description: For any measurable function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$ and real numbers $a, b$, the interval integral $\int_a^b f(x) \, d\mu$ is either equal to $\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu$ or to its negation $-\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu$, where $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b)]$ denotes the interval between $a$ and $b$.
Signature:  (f : ℝ → E) (a b) : (∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ) ∈ ({∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ, -∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ} : Set E)

6. [THEOREM] Integral of the Constant Function 1: $\int_{a}^{b} 1 \, dx = b - a$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals
Name: integral_one
Description: The integral of the constant function $1$ over the interval $[a, b]$ is equal to the length of the interval, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} 1 \, dx = b - a. \]
Signature:  : (∫ _ in a..b, (1 : ℝ)) = b - a

7. [THEOREM] Scaled Integral Transformation: $c \cdot \int_{a}^{b} f(cx) \, dx = \int_{ac}^{bc} f(x) \, dx$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.smul_integral_comp_mul_right
Description: For any real number $c$ and any integrable function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$, the scaled integral $c \cdot \int_{a}^{b} f(x \cdot c) \, dx$ equals the integral of $f(x)$ over the scaled interval $[a \cdot c, b \cdot c]$, i.e.,
\[ c \cdot \int_{a}^{b} f(x \cdot c) \, dx = \int_{a \cdot c}^{b \cdot c} f(x) \, dx. \]
Signature:  (c) : (c • ∫ x in a..b, f (x * c)) = ∫ x in a * c..b * c, f x

1. [THEOREM] Norm Bound for Interval Integral under Almost Everywhere Constraint: $\|\int_a^b f\| \leq C|b-a|$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const_ae
Description: For any real numbers $a, b$ and any function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$, if there exists a constant $C$ such that $\|f(x)\| \leq C$ for almost every $x$ in the interval $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b)]$, then the norm of the integral of $f$ over $[a,b]$ satisfies
\[ \left\| \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, dx \right\| \leq C \cdot |b - a|. \]
Signature:  {a b C : ℝ} {f : ℝ → E} (h : ∀ᵐ x, x ∈ Ι a b → ‖f x‖ ≤ C) : ‖∫ x in a..b, f x‖ ≤ C * |b - a|

2. [THEOREM] Norm Equality for Interval Integrals: $\|\int_a^b f\| = \|\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f\|$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.norm_intervalIntegral_eq
Description: For any real numbers $a$ and $b$ and any measurable function $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$, the norm of the interval integral $\|\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu\|$ is equal to the norm of the integral of $f$ over the interval $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b)]$, i.e.,
\[ \left\|\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu\right\| = \left\|\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu\right\|. \]
Signature:  (f : ℝ → E) (a b : ℝ) (μ : Measure ℝ) : ‖∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ‖ = ‖∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ‖

3. [THEOREM] Norm Bound for Interval Integral: $\|\int_a^b f\| \leq C|b-a|$ under Uniform Constraint
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const
Description: For any real numbers $a, b$, any function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$, and any constant $C \in \mathbb{R}$, if $\|f(x)\| \leq C$ for all $x$ in the interval $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b))$, then the norm of the integral of $f$ over $[a,b]$ satisfies
\[ \left\| \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, dx \right\| \leq C \cdot |b - a|. \]
Signature:  {a b C : ℝ} {f : ℝ → E} (h : ∀ x ∈ Ι a b, ‖f x‖ ≤ C) : ‖∫ x in a..b, f x‖ ≤ C * |b - a|

