1. [THEOREM] Interval integrability criterion for $a \leq b$: $f$ integrable on $[a,b]$ iff integrable on $(a,b]$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegrable_iff_integrableOn_Ioc_of_le
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$, a function $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$ is interval integrable with respect to measure $\mu$ on $[a, b]$ if and only if $f$ is integrable on the half-open interval $(a, b]$ with respect to $\mu$.
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b ↔ IntegrableOn f (Ioc a b) μ

2. [THEOREM] Nonnegativity of Interval Integral Under Almost Everywhere Nonnegative Condition
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_nonneg_of_ae
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$ and any measurable function $f$ with respect to a measure $\mu$, if $f$ is almost everywhere nonnegative (i.e., $0 \leq f(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x \in \mathbb{R}$), then the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ is nonnegative, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu \geq 0. \]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : 0 ≤ᵐ[μ] f) : 0 ≤ ∫ u in a..b, f u ∂μ

3. [THEOREM] Nonnegativity of Interval Integral Under Almost Everywhere Nonnegative Condition on $[a,b]$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_nonneg_of_ae_restrict
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$ and any measurable function $f$ with respect to a measure $\mu$, if $f$ is almost everywhere nonnegative on the closed interval $[a, b]$ (i.e., $0 \leq f(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x \in [a, b]$), then the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ is nonnegative, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu \geq 0. \]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : 0 ≤ᵐ[μ.restrict (Icc a b)] f) : 0 ≤ ∫ u in a..b, f u ∂μ

1. [THEOREM] Nonnegativity of Set Integral Under Almost Everywhere Nonnegative Condition
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.SetIntegral
Name: MeasureTheory.setIntegral_nonneg_of_ae_restrict
Description: For any measurable function $f$ and measurable set $s$ with respect to a measure $\mu$, if $f$ is almost everywhere nonnegative on $s$ (i.e., $0 \leq f(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x \in s$), then the integral of $f$ over $s$ is nonnegative, i.e.,
\[ \int_{x \in s} f(x) \, d\mu \geq 0. \]
Signature:  (hf : 0 ≤ᵐ[μ.restrict s] f) : 0 ≤ ∫ x in s, f x ∂μ

