1. [THEOREM] Nonnegativity of Interval Integral Under Almost Everywhere Nonnegative Condition on $[a,b]$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_nonneg_of_ae_restrict
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$ and any measurable function $f$ with respect to a measure $\mu$, if $f$ is almost everywhere nonnegative on the closed interval $[a, b]$ (i.e., $0 \leq f(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x \in [a, b]$), then the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ is nonnegative, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu \geq 0. \]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : 0 ≤ᵐ[μ.restrict (Icc a b)] f) : 0 ≤ ∫ u in a..b, f u ∂μ

2. [THEOREM] Monotonicity of interval integral under almost everywhere inequality on $[a,b]$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_mono_ae_restrict
Description: Let $f$ and $g$ be measurable functions on $\mathbb{R}$ with respect to a measure $\mu$. If $f \leq g$ holds almost everywhere on the closed interval $[a, b]$ with respect to the restricted measure $\mu \restrict [a, b]$, then the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ is less than or equal to the interval integral of $g$ from $a$ to $b$, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(u) \, d\mu \leq \int_{a}^{b} g(u) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  (h : f ≤ᵐ[μ.restrict (Icc a b)] g) : (∫ u in a..b, f u ∂μ) ≤ ∫ u in a..b, g u ∂μ

3. [THEOREM] Strict inequality for integrals: $\int_a^b f < \int_a^b g$ when $f \leq g$ and $f < g$ on a set of positive measure
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_lt_integral_of_ae_le_of_measure_setOf_lt_ne_zero
Description: Let $f, g \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$ be interval integrable functions with respect to a measure $\mu$ on $[a,b]$, where $a \leq b$. If $f(x) \leq g(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x$ in the half-open interval $(a,b]$, and the set $\{x \in (a,b] \mid f(x) < g(x)\}$ has positive $\mu$-measure, then the integral of $f$ over $[a,b]$ is strictly less than the integral of $g$ over the same interval, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu < \int_{a}^{b} g(x) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hfi : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b) (hgi : IntervalIntegrable g μ a b)
  (hle : f ≤ᵐ[μ.restrict (Ioc a b)] g) (hlt : μ.restrict (Ioc a b) {x | f x < g x} ≠ 0) :
  (∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ) < ∫ x in a..b, g x ∂μ

