Description: For a constant function $f(x) = C$ where $C$ is an element of a normed space $E$, and a measure $\mu$ on a measurable space, the function $f$ is integrable on a set $s$ with respect to $\mu$ if and only if either $C = 0$ or the measure $\mu$ is finite on $s$ (i.e., $\mu(s) < \infty$).
Signature:  {C : E} : IntegrableOn (fun _ => C) s μ ↔ C = 0 ∨ μ s < ∞

5. [THEOREM] Monotonicity of Lower Lebesgue Integral with Respect to Pointwise Inequality
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Lebesgue
Name: MeasureTheory.lintegral_mono_fn
Description: For any measurable functions $f, g \colon \alpha \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\infty\}$ such that $f(x) \leq g(x)$ for all $x \in \alpha$, the lower Lebesgue integrals satisfy:
\[
\int⁻_a f(a) \, d\mu \leq \int⁻_a g(a) \, d\mu.
\]
Signature:  ⦃f g : α → ℝ≥0∞⦄ (hfg : ∀ x, f x ≤ g x) : ∫⁻ a, f a ∂μ ≤ ∫⁻ a, g a ∂μ

1. [THEOREM] Monotonicity of interval integral under almost everywhere inequality
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_mono_ae
Description: Let $f$ and $g$ be measurable functions on $\mathbb{R}$ with respect to a measure $\mu$. If $f \leq g$ holds almost everywhere with respect to $\mu$, then for any real numbers $a$ and $b$, the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ is less than or equal to the interval integral of $g$ from $a$ to $b$, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(u) \, d\mu \leq \int_{a}^{b} g(u) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  (h : f ≤ᵐ[μ] g) : (∫ u in a..b, f u ∂μ) ≤ ∫ u in a..b, g u ∂μ

2. [THEOREM] Monotonicity of interval integral under almost everywhere inequality on $[a,b]$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_mono_ae_restrict
Description: Let $f$ and $g$ be measurable functions on $\mathbb{R}$ with respect to a measure $\mu$. If $f \leq g$ holds almost everywhere on the closed interval $[a, b]$ with respect to the restricted measure $\mu \restrict [a, b]$, then the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ is less than or equal to the interval integral of $g$ from $a$ to $b$, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(u) \, d\mu \leq \int_{a}^{b} g(u) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  (h : f ≤ᵐ[μ.restrict (Icc a b)] g) : (∫ u in a..b, f u ∂μ) ≤ ∫ u in a..b, g u ∂μ
