1. [THEOREM] Integral over subset is bounded by full integral for nonnegative functions
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.SetIntegral
Name: MeasureTheory.setIntegral_le_integral
Description: For any integrable function $f$ on a measure space $(X, \mu)$ that is nonnegative almost everywhere with respect to $\mu$, the integral of $f$ over any measurable set $s$ is less than or equal to the integral of $f$ over the entire space. That is,
\[ \int_{x \in s} f(x) \, d\mu \leq \int_{x} f(x) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  (hfi : Integrable f μ) (hf : 0 ≤ᵐ[μ] f) : ∫ x in s, f x ∂μ ≤ ∫ x, f x ∂μ

2. [THEOREM] Nonnegativity of Set Integral Under Almost Everywhere Nonnegative Condition
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.SetIntegral
Name: MeasureTheory.setIntegral_nonneg_of_ae_restrict
Description: For any measurable function $f$ and measurable set $s$ with respect to a measure $\mu$, if $f$ is almost everywhere nonnegative on $s$ (i.e., $0 \leq f(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x \in s$), then the integral of $f$ over $s$ is nonnegative, i.e.,
\[ \int_{x \in s} f(x) \, d\mu \geq 0. \]
Signature:  (hf : 0 ≤ᵐ[μ.restrict s] f) : 0 ≤ ∫ x in s, f x ∂μ

3. [DEFINITION] Closed interval $[a, b]$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Set.Defs
Name: Set.Icc
Description: For elements $a$ and $b$ in a preorder $\alpha$, the set $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ is defined as the closed interval $[a, b]$, consisting of all elements $x$ satisfying $a \leq x \leq b$.
Signature:  (a b : α)

