Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.SetIntegral
Name: MeasureTheory.setIntegral_nonneg_of_ae
Description: For any measurable function $f$ and any measurable set $s$ with respect to a measure $\mu$, if $f$ is almost everywhere nonnegative with respect to $\mu$ (i.e., $0 \leq f(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x$), then the integral of $f$ over $s$ is nonnegative, i.e.,
