Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.SetIntegral
Name: MeasureTheory.integral_indicator_const
Description: For any complete space $E$ and constant $e \in E$, and for any measurable set $s$, the integral of the indicator function of $s$ applied to the constant function $x \mapsto e$ over the whole space equals the scalar product of the measure $\mu(s)$ (converted to a real number) and $e$. That is,
