Signature:  (h : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b) : IntegrableOn f (Ι a b) μ

4. [THEOREM] Interval integrability is preserved under division by a scalar
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: IntervalIntegrable.div_const
Description: Let $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{K}$ be a function that is interval integrable with respect to a measure $\mu$ on $[a, b]$, where $\mathbb{K}$ is a normed field. Then for any nonzero $c \in \mathbb{K}$, the function $x \mapsto f(x) / c$ is interval integrable on $[a, b]$ with respect to $\mu$.
Signature:  {𝕜 : Type*} {f : ℝ → 𝕜} [NormedField 𝕜] (h : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b) (c : 𝕜) :
  IntervalIntegrable (fun x => f x / c) μ a b

5. [THEOREM] Integrability on Closed Interval Implies Interval Integrability
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: MeasureTheory.IntegrableOn.intervalIntegrable
Description: If a function $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$ is integrable on the closed interval $[a, b]$ with respect to a measure $\mu$, then $f$ is interval integrable on $[a, b]$ with respect to $\mu$, i.e., $f$ is integrable on both $(a, b]$ and $(b, a]$.
Signature:  (hf : IntegrableOn f [[a, b]] μ) : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b

