2. [DEFINITION] Restriction of a partial value
Module: Mathlib.Data.Part
Name: Part.restrict
Description: Given a proposition `p` and a partial value `o : Part α` with a proof that `p` implies `o` is defined (i.e., `H : p → o.Dom`), the restriction `Part.restrict p o H` constructs a new partial value with domain `p` whose value (when `p` holds) is equal to the value of `o`.

More formally, for any `a : α`, we have `a ∈ Part.restrict p o H` if and only if `p` holds and `a ∈ o`.
