1. [THEOREM] Almost Everywhere Equivalence between Measure Restriction and Subtype Pullback: $(\forallᵐ x \, \mu|_s, p(x)) \leftrightarrow (\forallᵐ x \, \iota^*\mu, p(x))$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Restrict
Name: ae_restrict_iff_subtype
Description: Let $(α, \mathcal{M}, μ)$ be a measure space, $s \subseteq α$ a measurable subset, and $p \colon α \to \mathrm{Prop}$ a property. Then the following are equivalent:
1. $p(x)$ holds for $μ|_s$-almost every $x \in α$.
2. $p(x)$ holds for $\iota^*μ$-almost every $x \in s$, where $\iota \colon s \hookrightarrow α$ is the inclusion map.
Signature:  {m0 : MeasurableSpace α} {μ : Measure α} {s : Set α} (hs : MeasurableSet s) {p : α → Prop} :
  (∀ᵐ x ∂μ.restrict s, p x) ↔ ∀ᵐ (x : s) ∂comap ((↑) : s → α) μ, p x
