Signature:  {s : Set X} (hs : MeasurableSet s) (hf : StronglyMeasurable f) (hfi : Integrable f μ) :
  ∫ x in s, f x ∂μ ≤ ∫ x in {y | 0 ≤ f y}, f x ∂μ

2. [THEOREM] Almost Everywhere Inequality from Set Integral Inequalities
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.AEEqOfIntegral
Name: MeasureTheory.ae_le_of_forall_setIntegral_le
Description: Let $f, g \colon \alpha \to \mathbb{R}$ be integrable functions with respect to a measure $\mu$ on a measurable space $\alpha$. If for every measurable set $s$ with $\mu(s) < \infty$, the integral of $f$ over $s$ is less than or equal to the integral of $g$ over $s$, then $f \leq g$ almost everywhere with respect to $\mu$, i.e., $f(x) \leq g(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x \in \alpha$.
Signature:  {f g : α → ℝ} (hf : Integrable f μ) (hg : Integrable g μ)
  (hf_le : ∀ s, MeasurableSet s → μ s < ∞ → (∫ x in s, f x ∂μ) ≤ ∫ x in s, g x ∂μ) : f ≤ᵐ[μ] g

3. [THEOREM] Integral over subset is bounded by full integral for nonnegative functions
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.SetIntegral
Name: MeasureTheory.setIntegral_le_integral
Description: For any integrable function $f$ on a measure space $(X, \mu)$ that is nonnegative almost everywhere with respect to $\mu$, the integral of $f$ over any measurable set $s$ is less than or equal to the integral of $f$ over the entire space. That is,
\[ \int_{x \in s} f(x) \, d\mu \leq \int_{x} f(x) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  (hfi : Integrable f μ) (hf : 0 ≤ᵐ[μ] f) : ∫ x in s, f x ∂μ ≤ ∫ x, f x ∂μ

4. [THEOREM] Infimum Inequality for Lower Lebesgue Integral of Pointwise Infimum
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Lebesgue
Name: MeasureTheory.le_iInf₂_lintegral
Description: For any family of measurable functions $f_i^h \colon \alpha \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\infty\}$ indexed by $i$ and $h \in \iota'_i$, the lower Lebesgue integral of the pointwise infimum of these functions is bounded above by the infimum of their integrals. That is,
\[
\int⁻_a \left( \inf_{i} \inf_{h \in \iota'_i} f_i^h(a) \right) d\mu \leq \inf_{i} \inf_{h \in \iota'_i} \left( \int⁻_a f_i^h(a) d\mu \right).
\]
Signature:  {ι : Sort*} {ι' : ι → Sort*} (f : ∀ i, ι' i → α → ℝ≥0∞) :
  ∫⁻ a, ⨅ (i) (h : ι' i), f i h a ∂μ ≤ ⨅ (i) (h : ι' i), ∫⁻ a, f i h a ∂μ

5. [THEOREM] Inequality between integrals with density and product measures: $\int g \, d(\mu \text{ with density } f) \leq \int (f \cdot g) \, d\mu$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.WithDensity
Name: MeasureTheory.lintegral_withDensity_le_lintegral_mul
Description: Let $\mu$ be a measure on a measurable space $\alpha$ and let $f \colon \alpha \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\infty\}$ be a measurable function. For any function $g \colon \alpha \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\infty\}$, the integral of $g$ with respect to the measure $\mu.\text{withDensity}\, f$ is bounded above by the integral of the pointwise product $f \cdot g$ with respect to $\mu$:
\[
\int^-_a g(a) \, d(\mu.\text{withDensity}\, f) \leq \int^-_a f(a) g(a) \, d\mu.
\]
Signature:  (μ : Measure α) {f : α → ℝ≥0∞} (f_meas : Measurable f) (g : α → ℝ≥0∞) :
  (∫⁻ a, g a ∂μ.withDensity f) ≤ ∫⁻ a, (f * g) a ∂μ

