\[ \int_{x \in s} f(x) \, d\mu \leq \int_{x} f(x) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  (hfi : Integrable f μ) (hf : 0 ≤ᵐ[μ] f) : ∫ x in s, f x ∂μ ≤ ∫ x, f x ∂μ

2. [THEOREM] Nonnegativity of Set Integral Under Almost Everywhere Nonnegative Condition
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.SetIntegral
Name: MeasureTheory.setIntegral_nonneg_of_ae_restrict
Description: For any measurable function $f$ and measurable set $s$ with respect to a measure $\mu$, if $f$ is almost everywhere nonnegative on $s$ (i.e., $0 \leq f(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x \in s$), then the integral of $f$ over $s$ is nonnegative, i.e.,
\[ \int_{x \in s} f(x) \, d\mu \geq 0. \]
Signature:  (hf : 0 ≤ᵐ[μ.restrict s] f) : 0 ≤ ∫ x in s, f x ∂μ

3. [THEOREM] Almost Everywhere Property Preservation under Measure Restriction
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Restrict
Name: MeasureTheory.ae_restrict_of_ae
Description: Let $\mu$ be a measure on a measurable space $\alpha$ and let $s \subseteq \alpha$ be a subset. If a property $p(x)$ holds for $\mu$-almost every $x \in \alpha$, then $p(x)$ also holds for $\mu|_s$-almost every $x \in \alpha$, where $\mu|_s$ denotes the restriction of $\mu$ to $s$.
Signature:  {s : Set α} {p : α → Prop} (h : ∀ᵐ x ∂μ, p x) : ∀ᵐ x ∂μ.restrict s, p x

4. [THEOREM] Almost Everywhere Property Preservation under Measure Restriction and Subset Inclusion
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Restrict
Name: MeasureTheory.ae_restrict_of_ae_restrict_of_subset
Description: Let $\mu$ be a measure on a measurable space $\alpha$, and let $s, t \subseteq \alpha$ be subsets with $s \subseteq t$. If a property $p(x)$ holds for $\mu|_t$-almost every $x \in \alpha$, then $p(x)$ also holds for $\mu|_s$-almost every $x \in \alpha$, where $\mu|_s$ and $\mu|_t$ denote the restrictions of $\mu$ to $s$ and $t$ respectively.
Signature:  {s t : Set α} {p : α → Prop} (hst : s ⊆ t) (h : ∀ᵐ x ∂μ.restrict t, p x) : ∀ᵐ x ∂μ.restrict s, p x

