6. [THEOREM] Strict inequality for integrals: $\int_a^b f < \int_a^b g$ when $f \leq g$ and $f < g$ on a set of positive measure
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_lt_integral_of_ae_le_of_measure_setOf_lt_ne_zero
Description: Let $f, g \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$ be interval integrable functions with respect to a measure $\mu$ on $[a,b]$, where $a \leq b$. If $f(x) \leq g(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x$ in the half-open interval $(a,b]$, and the set $\{x \in (a,b] \mid f(x) < g(x)\}$ has positive $\mu$-measure, then the integral of $f$ over $[a,b]$ is strictly less than the integral of $g$ over the same interval, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu < \int_{a}^{b} g(x) \, d\mu. \]
