2. [THEOREM] Interval integral over ordered endpoints equals integral over half-open interval
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_of_le
Description: For any real numbers $a$ and $b$ with $a \leq b$, the interval integral $\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu$ is equal to the integral of $f$ over the half-open interval $(a, b]$, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu = \int_{(a,b]} f(x) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  (h : a ≤ b) : ∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ = ∫ x in Ioc a b, f x ∂μ

3. [THEOREM] Integral of Constant Function over Interval with General Measure
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_const'
Description: Let $E$ be a complete space and $c \in E$ be a constant. The integral of the constant function $x \mapsto c$ over the interval $[a, b]$ with respect to measure $\mu$ is given by:
\[ \int_{x \in a..b} c \, d\mu = \big(\mu(\text{Ioc}(a,b))_{\text{toReal}} - \mu(\text{Ioc}(b,a))_{\text{toReal}}\big) \cdot c, \]
where $\text{Ioc}(a,b)$ denotes the half-open interval $(a, b]$.
Signature:  [CompleteSpace E] (c : E) : ∫ _ in a..b, c ∂μ = ((μ <| Ioc a b).toReal - (μ <| Ioc b a).toReal) • c

