2. [THEOREM] Set Integral is Bounded by Integral Over Nonnegative Part
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.SetIntegral
Name: MeasureTheory.setIntegral_le_nonneg
Description: For any measurable set $s$ and strongly measurable function $f$ that is integrable with respect to measure $\mu$, the integral of $f$ over $s$ is less than or equal to the integral of $f$ over the set $\{y \mid 0 \leq f(y)\}$. That is,
\[ \int_{x \in s} f(x) \, d\mu \leq \int_{x \in \{y \mid 0 \leq f(y)\}} f(x) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  {s : Set X} (hs : MeasurableSet s) (hf : StronglyMeasurable f) (hfi : Integrable f μ) :
  ∫ x in s, f x ∂μ ≤ ∫ x in {y | 0 ≤ f y}, f x ∂μ

3. [THEOREM] Almost Everywhere Inequality from Set Integral Inequalities
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.AEEqOfIntegral
Name: MeasureTheory.ae_le_of_forall_setIntegral_le
Description: Let $f, g \colon \alpha \to \mathbb{R}$ be integrable functions with respect to a measure $\mu$ on a measurable space $\alpha$. If for every measurable set $s$ with $\mu(s) < \infty$, the integral of $f$ over $s$ is less than or equal to the integral of $g$ over $s$, then $f \leq g$ almost everywhere with respect to $\mu$, i.e., $f(x) \leq g(x)$ for $\mu$-almost every $x \in \alpha$.
Signature:  {f g : α → ℝ} (hf : Integrable f μ) (hg : Integrable g μ)
  (hf_le : ∀ s, MeasurableSet s → μ s < ∞ → (∫ x in s, f x ∂μ) ≤ ∫ x in s, g x ∂μ) : f ≤ᵐ[μ] g

