In notation:
- $\int⁻ x, f(x) \, d\mu$ denotes the integral with respect to measure $\mu$
- $\int⁻ x, f(x)$ denotes the integral with respect to the canonical volume measure
- $\int⁻ x \in s, f(x) \, d\mu$ denotes the integral over set $s$ with respect to $\mu$
- $\int⁻ x \in s, f(x)$ denotes the integral over set $s$ with respect to volume measure
