Name: MeasureTheory.lintegral
Description: The lower Lebesgue integral of a measurable function $f \colon \alpha \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\infty\}$ with respect to a measure $\mu$ is defined as the supremum of the integrals of all simple functions $g \colon \alpha \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\infty\}$ such that $g \leq f$ pointwise. 

In notation:
- $\int⁻ x, f(x) \, d\mu$ denotes the integral with respect to measure $\mu$
- $\int⁻ x, f(x)$ denotes the integral with respect to the canonical volume measure
- $\int⁻ x \in s, f(x) \, d\mu$ denotes the integral over set $s$ with respect to $\mu$
- $\int⁻ x \in s, f(x)$ denotes the integral over set $s$ with respect to volume measure
