5. [DEFINITION] Integral values of measurable functions dominated by $\nu$ with respect to $\mu$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Decomposition.Lebesgue
Name: MeasureTheory.Measure.LebesgueDecomposition.measurableLEEval
Description: For two measures $\mu$ and $\nu$ on a measurable space, the set $\text{measurableLEEval}\,\mu\,\nu$ consists of all values of the integral $\int⁻ x, f(x) \, d\mu$ for measurable functions $f$ in $\text{measurableLE}\,\mu\,\nu$, where $\text{measurableLE}\,\mu\,\nu$ is the set of measurable functions $f$ such that for every measurable set $A$, $\int_A f \, d\mu \leq \nu(A)$.

In symbols:
\[ \text{measurableLEEval}\,\mu\,\nu = \left\{ \int⁻ x, f(x) \, d\mu \mid f \in \text{measurableLE}\,\mu\,\nu \right\}. \]
