1. [THEOREM] Image of Closed Interval under Antitone Function is Contained in $[f(b), f(a)]$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Set.Image
Name: AntitoneOn.image_Icc_subset
Description: Let $f$ be a function defined on the closed interval $[a, b]$ in a preorder $\alpha$. If $f$ is antitone (i.e., decreasing) on $[a, b]$, then the image of $[a, b]$ under $f$ is contained in the closed interval $[f(b), f(a)]$.
Signature:  (h : AntitoneOn f (Icc a b)) : f '' Icc a b ⊆ Icc (f b) (f a)

2. [THEOREM] Image of Closed Interval under Antitone Function is $[f(b), f(a)]$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Set.Image
Name: AntitoneOn.mapsTo_Icc
Description: Let $f$ be a function defined on the closed interval $[a, b]$ in a preorder $\alpha$. If $f$ is antitone (i.e., decreasing) on $[a, b]$, then $f$ maps the interval $[a, b]$ to the closed interval $[f(b), f(a)]$.
Signature:  (h : AntitoneOn f (Icc a b)) : MapsTo f (Icc a b) (Icc (f b) (f a))

